{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BBcbc4MmxFu4sEHVyD4d6z","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tnarrative_guidance: '放弃三 Claim 结构，重构为单 claim 论文：''Debiasing Can Hurt — When Global\n2\t  Misclassification Correction Amplifies Subgroup CATE Bias''。Claim 1（bias identity\n3\t  + exact product form + constructive debiasing-hurts proposition）是唯一可靠的核心贡献。EC-HTE\n4\t  降级为 ''one possible mitigation''，诚实承认其优势条件极窄（仅 synthetic extreme + large n_expert）。诊断准则\n5\t  CV AUC 崩塌，重构为 sufficient condition for concern 而非 decision tool。Real data 反向结果不掩盖，\n6\t  作为 ''honest empirical assessment'' 呈现。论文变短、更聚焦、理论更强。投 EMNLP main，定位为 negative result\n7\t  + formal characterization 类型论文。预期需要 2R 或 resubmit。\n8\t\n9\t  '\n10\timagined_experiments:\n11\t- name: Hierarchical Bayesian EC-HTE synthetic validation\n12\t  plan_id: exp-001\n13\t  description: 'HB Dirichlet-prior confusion matrix estimator vs MLE/Laplace，full\n14\t    regime sweep。 Worst 档下 HB 改进微弱，RMSE penalty 显著，partial pooling 在多数配置无实质优势。\n15\t\n16\t    '\n17\t  expected_results:\n18\t    mcmc_rhat_max: 1.03\n19\t    mcmc_ess_min: 110\n20\t    mcmc_divergent: 0\n21\t    runtime_min: 85\n22\t    total_mc_runs: 3600\n23\t    hb_vs_mle_rmse_improvement_k2_n50: 1-3%\n24\t    hb_vs_mle_rmse_improvement_k2_n100: <1%\n25\t    hb_vs_mle_rmse_improvement_k4_n50_moderate: 2-4%\n26\t    hb_coverage_min: 0.85\n27\t    hb_coverage_median: 0.9\n28\t    k4_extreme_n50_blowup: true\n29\t    k4_extreme_n50_blowup_note: Singularity guard triggers frequently (~15% of runs);\n30\t      residual instability even with 4-chain MCMC\n31\t    hb_vs_global_rmse_median_penalty: 1.5\n32\t    hb_beats_global_pct: 35% of configs (only extreme regime + n>=500)\n33\t    hyperprior_sensitivity_k4_rmse_variation: 8-12%\n34\t    hyperprior_sensitivity_conclusion: moderate sensitivity — k4 results shift meaningfully\n35\t      with scale\n36\t  result_rationale: 'Worst 档核心假设是 EC-HTE 优势微弱。HB partial pooling 在 moderate regime\n37\t    几乎无 改进（heterogeneity 不足以让 stratification 获益），extreme regime 仅在 n_expert 足够大时才有意义。K=4\n38\t    时 per-subgroup 样本太少（n_expert/4），CM 估计噪声高，HB shrinkage 不足以补偿。MCMC 收敛勉强合格但 ESS 偏低，说明后验几何复杂。Hyperprior\n39\t    sensitivity 在 K=4 时较高，因为 Dirichlet concentration 对稀疏子群影响大。整体结论： HB 是一个 marginal\n40\t    improvement over MLE，不构成独立贡献。\n41\t\n42\t    '\n43\t  tables:\n44\t  - title: 'Table 1: HB vs MLE vs Global RMSE across regime × K × n_expert'\n45\t    columns:\n46\t    - regime\n47\t    - K\n48\t    - n_expert\n49\t    - naive_rmse\n50\t    - global_rmse\n51\t    - mle_rmse\n52\t    - hb_rmse\n53\t    - hb_vs_global_pct\n54\t    representative_rows:\n55\t    - - extreme\n56\t      - 2\n57\t      - 100\n58\t      - 0.18\n59\t      - 0.15\n60\t      - 0.17\n61\t      - 0.16\n62\t      - +6.7%\n63\t    - - extreme\n64\t      - 2\n65\t      - 500\n66\t      - 0.18\n67\t      - 0.15\n68\t      - 0.13\n69\t      - 0.13\n70\t      - -13.3%\n71\t    - - extreme\n72\t      - 4\n73\t      - 100\n74\t      - 0.2\n75\t      - 0.16\n76\t      - 0.25\n77\t      - 0.23\n78\t      - +43.8%\n79\t    - - extreme\n80\t      - 4\n81\t      - 500\n82\t      - 0.2\n83\t      - 0.16\n84\t      - 0.16\n85\t      - 0.15\n86\t      - -6.3%\n87\t    - - moderate\n88\t      - 2\n89\t      - 100\n90\t      - 0.14\n91\t      - 0.12\n92\t      - 0.13\n93\t      - 0.13\n94\t      - +8.3%\n95\t    - - moderate\n96\t      - 2\n97\t      - 500\n98\t      - 0.14\n99\t      - 0.12\n100\t      - 0.12\n101\t      - 0.12\n102\t      - 0%\n103\t    - - moderate\n104\t      - 4\n105\t      - 100\n106\t      - 0.16\n107\t      - 0.13\n108\t      - 0.19\n109\t      - 0.18\n110\t      - +38.5%\n111\t    - - moderate\n112\t      - 4\n113\t      - 500\n114\t      - 0.16\n115\t      - 0.13\n116\t      - 0.14\n117\t      - 0.13\n118\t      - 0%\n119\t  figures_description:\n120\t  - 'Heatmap: HB vs Global RMSE ratio across n_expert × K grid. 大面积 >1.0（红色），仅右下角（high\n121\t    n, extreme）<1.0（蓝色）'\n122\t  analysis: 'EC-HTE 在多数实际配置下 RMSE 劣于 global。Partial pooling 的 James-Stein 优势 被 per-subgroup\n123\t    CM 估计噪声淹没。仅在 extreme heterogeneity + n_expert >= 500 时 才有 RMSE 优势。这决定了 worst 档叙事：EC-HTE\n124\t    不能作为 standalone contribution， 只能作为 conditional mitigation 附在 bias mechanism 主线之后。\n125\t\n126\t    '\n127\t- name: Formal bias identity verification\n128\t  plan_id: exp-002\n129\t  description: 'Bias = Δπ × Δτ product form 的 analytic derivation + MC 验证。Worst 档下\n130\t    identity 本身成立（这是数学事实），但 amplification magnitude 处于范围低端。\n131\t\n132\t    '\n133\t  expected_results:\n134\t    r2_k2: 0.99\n135\t    r2_k4: 0.965\n136\t    tightness_ratio_k2_median: 1.005\n137\t    tightness_ratio_k4_median: 1.035\n138\t    debiasing_hurts_pct: 48\n139\t    debiasing_hurts_pct_note: 略低于 50%，因为 MC noise 在 boundary 附近导致一些 marginal cases\n140\t      翻转\n141\t    max_bias_ratio_k2: 2.5\n142\t    max_bias_ratio_k4: 2.4\n143\t    coverage_2se_k2: 0.945\n144\t    coverage_2se_k4: 0.93\n145\t    bias_amplification_median_across_configs: 1.4\n146\t  result_rationale: 'Bias identity 是精确等式（population level），R² 接近 1.0 是数学保证，worst 档无法\n147\t    改变这一点。但 worst 档体现在 amplification magnitude 偏低端：K=2 max 2.5×（而非 2.86×），K=4 max\n148\t    2.4×（而非 2.41×）。这是因为 worst 档假设 moderate regime 占更多 权重——当 Δπ 和 Δτ 都不极端时，amplification\n149\t    存在但不dramatic。Debiasing hurts 的 比例约 48%（接近 coin-flip），审稿人可能认为这不足以构成 ''alarming\n150\t    finding''。K=4 的 R² 稍低反映了 sum-of-products form 在有限样本下的噪声放大。关键问题不在于 identity 是否成立（它一定成立），而在于\n151\t    amplification 的实际幅度是否足以让审稿人认为这是 a problem worth solving。\n152\t\n153\t    '\n154\t  tables:\n155\t  - title: 'Table 2: Bias amplification ratio across Δπ × Δτ grid (K=2)'\n156\t    columns:\n157\t    - delta_pi\n158\t    - delta_tau\n159\t    - analytic_bias\n160\t    - mc_bias_mean\n161\t    - mc_bias_se\n162\t    - amplification_ratio\n163\t    representative_rows:\n164\t    - - 0.05\n165\t      - 0.1\n166\t      - 0.005\n167\t      - 0.006\n168\t      - 0.002\n169\t      - 1.1\n170\t    - - 0.1\n171\t      - 0.2\n172\t      - 0.02\n173\t      - 0.021\n174\t      - 0.004\n175\t      - 1.4\n176\t    - - 0.15\n177\t      - 0.3\n178\t      - 0.045\n179\t      - 0.046\n180\t      - 0.006\n181\t      - 1.8\n182\t    - - 0.2\n183\t      - 0.5\n184\t      - 0.1\n185\t      - 0.098\n186\t      - 0.008\n187\t      - 2.5\n188\t  - title: 'Table 3: Debiasing-hurts breakdown by parameter region'\n189\t    columns:\n190\t    - region\n191\t    - n_settings\n192\t    - hurts_pct\n193\t    - max_ratio\n194\t    - median_ratio\n195\t    representative_rows:\n196\t    - - extreme (Δπ>0.15, Δτ>0.3)\n197\t      - 40\n198\t      - 85\n199\t      - 2.5\n200\t      - 1.8\n201\t    - - moderate (0.05<Δπ<0.15)\n202\t      - 120\n203\t      - 52\n204\t      - 1.5\n205\t      - 1.1\n206\t    - - low (Δπ<0.05)\n207\t      - 100\n208\t      - 12\n209\t      - 1.05\n210\t      - 1.0\n211\t  figures_description:\n212\t  - 'Heatmap: amplification ratio as function of Δπ × Δτ. 颜色梯度从 1.0（白）到 2.5（深红）。高\n213\t    amplification 区域集中在右上角但面积有限。'\n214\t  - 'Scatter: analytic prediction vs MC observed bias, R²=0.990(K=2) / 0.965(K=4).\n215\t    对角线拟合良好。'\n216\t  analysis: 'Bias identity 验证成功——这是 worst 档唯一完全 robust 的结果。但 amplification 幅度在 moderate\n217\t    regime 仅 1.1-1.5×，审稿人可能认为 ''debiasing hurts by 10-50% is a known risk, not a new\n218\t    discovery''。Worst 档叙事必须强调 extreme regime 的 2.5× amplification 和 constructive example，同时承认\n219\t    moderate regime 的 effect size 较小。 Carroll et al. (2006) 的 qualitative insight\n220\t    已覆盖 ''correction can amplify error'' 的概念；我们的 quantitative product form 是增量贡献而非\n221\t    breakthrough。\n222\t\n223\t    '\n224\t- name: Semi-synthetic benchmark (TweetEval sentiment)\n225\t  plan_id: exp-003\n226\t  description: 'TweetEval sentiment 语料上注入 CATE heterogeneity，GPT-4.1 annotation，EC-HTE\n227\t    vs baselines。Worst 档下 EC-HTE 在 semi-synthetic 上优势微弱，RMSE penalty 大。\n228\t\n229\t    '\n230\t  expected_results:\n231\t    n_subgroups: 4\n232\t    misclass_rates: S0=0.08, S1=0.12, S2=0.14, S3=0.22\n233\t    delta_pi: 0.14\n234\t    mc_runs: 100\n235\t    avg_abs_bias:\n236\t      oracle: 0.005\n237\t      naive: 0.12\n238\t      global_corrected: 0.09\n239\t      stratified_mle: 0.07\n240\t      hb_ec_hte: 0.065\n241\t    avg_rmse:\n242\t      oracle: 0.04\n243\t      naive: 0.15\n244\t      global_corrected: 0.12\n245\t      stratified_mle: 0.18\n246\t      hb_ec_hte: 0.16\n247\t    ec_hte_bias_reduction_vs_global: 1.38\n248\t    ec_hte_rmse_penalty_vs_global: 1.33\n249\t    hb_vs_mle_n100_S3: -5% RMSE (HB slightly worse)\n250\t    hb_vs_mle_n250_S3: +8% RMSE (HB slightly better)\n251\t    coverage_hb_overall: 0.91\n252\t    debiasing_hurts_confirmed: true\n253\t    debiasing_hurts_subgroups: S0, S1 (low-error subgroups over-corrected)\n254\t  result_rationale: 'Worst 档假设 ec_hte_bias_reduction_factor_vs_global 在 [0.8, 1.5]\n255\t    范围。这里取 1.38——EC-HTE 比 global 好 28% 在 bias 上，但 RMSE 代价 33%。Semi-synthetic 的 Δπ=0.14（moderate-to-high），足够让\n256\t    bias mechanism 可见但不足以让 EC-HTE 在 RMSE 上胜出。HB 在 n=100 时对 minority subgroup S3 仍然\n257\t    noisy（12.5 experts/subgroup for K=4），partial pooling 不够补偿。审稿人看到 bias 降了但 RMSE\n258\t    升了，会问 ''is this a net improvement?''——答案在 worst 档下是 ambiguous。Coverage 0.91 勉强\n259\t    acceptable 但不 impressive。关键：debiasing hurts 在 S0/S1 上仍然可见，这支持 Claim 1 叙事。\n260\t\n261\t    '\n262\t  tables:\n263\t  - title: 'Table 4: Semi-synthetic results by subgroup (n_expert=250, K=4)'\n264\t    columns:\n265\t    - subgroup\n266\t    - misclass_rate\n267\t    - naive_bias\n268\t    - global_bias\n269\t    - ec_hte_bias\n270\t    - ec_hte_rmse\n271\t    - global_rmse\n272\t    representative_rows:\n273\t    - - S0\n274\t      - 0.08\n275\t      - 0.02\n276\t      - 0.07\n277\t      - 0.03\n278\t      - 0.14\n279\t      - 0.1\n280\t    - - S1\n281\t      - 0.12\n282\t      - 0.05\n283\t      - 0.06\n284\t      - 0.04\n285\t      - 0.13\n286\t      - 0.1\n287\t    - - S2\n288\t      - 0.14\n289\t      - 0.08\n290\t      - 0.04\n291\t      - 0.03\n292\t      - 0.15\n293\t      - 0.11\n294\t    - - S3\n295\t      - 0.22\n296\t      - 0.15\n297\t      - 0.1\n298\t      - 0.06\n299\t      - 0.22\n300\t      - 0.16\n301\t  - title: 'Table 5: Bias-RMSE tradeoff summary across n_expert'\n302\t    columns:\n303\t    - n_expert\n304\t    - ec_hte_wins_bias\n305\t    - ec_hte_wins_rmse\n306\t    - net_ambiguous\n307\t    representative_rows:\n308\t    - - 100\n309\t      - 3/4 subgroups\n310\t      - 0/4 subgroups\n311\t      - 4/4\n312\t    - - 250\n313\t      - 4/4 subgroups\n314\t      - 1/4 subgroups\n315\t      - 3/4\n316\t    - - 500\n317\t      - 4/4 subgroups\n318\t      - 2/4 subgroups\n319\t      - 2/4\n320\t  figures_description:\n321\t  - 'Bar chart: |bias| by method × subgroup. EC-HTE bars consistently shorter but\n322\t    difference modest.'\n323\t  - 'Scatter: bias reduction vs RMSE penalty per config. 多数点在 ''bias better, RMSE\n324\t    worse'' 象限。'\n325\t  analysis: 'Semi-synthetic 结果支持 Claim 1（debiasing hurts 在 S0/S1 可见）但不支持 EC-HTE 作为\n326\t    strong solution。Bias-RMSE tradeoff 在多数配置下 ambiguous——审稿人会引用 ''reduces bias but\n327\t    increases MSE — net negative in practice''。Worst 档叙事：这些 结果 honestly show EC-HTE\n328\t    的条件性优势，论文重心应放在 bias mechanism discovery 而非 EC-HTE method contribution。\n329\t\n330\t    '\n331\t- name: Real-data case study (UC Berkeley Hate Speech)\n332\t  plan_id: exp-004\n333\t  description: 'UC Berkeley Measuring Hate Speech 数据集上的 pattern consistency 分析。Worst\n334\t    档下 EC-HTE 比 global 差——real data 反向。\n335\t\n336\t    '\n337\t  expected_results:\n338\t    dataset: UC Berkeley Measuring Hate Speech\n339\t    n_comments: 2496\n340\t    subgroups: platform_group × text_length (4 groups)\n341\t    delta_pi: 0.1\n342\t    global_FPR: 0.15\n343\t    global_FNR: 0.55\n344\t    avg_abs_bias:\n345\t      naive: 0.22\n346\t      global: 0.28\n347\t      ec_hte: 0.32\n348\t    ec_hte_minus_global_abs_bias: 0.04\n349\t    bootstrap_ci_ec_hte_minus_global: '[-0.02, 0.10]'\n350\t    cate_direction_consistency: 2/4 subgroups consistent with domain knowledge\n351\t    ec_hte_ci_width_median: 0.35\n352\t    global_ci_width_median: 0.22\n353\t  result_rationale: 'Worst 档核心假设之一：real data 持续显示 EC-HTE 比 global 差（|bias| 差距 ~0.04）。\n354\t    原因是多方面的：(1) 高 FNR (~55%) 意味着 confusion matrix 接近 singular，逆矩阵 amplifies estimation\n355\t    noise；(2) 仅 2496 samples 分 4 subgroups，per-subgroup expert labels 不足（~600/group，但\n356\t    CM 估计仍 noisy）；(3) text-feature subgroups 可能不对应 true misclassification heterogeneity\n357\t    structure（misspecified subgroups）； (4) Δπ=0.10 处于 moderate 范围，stratification 收益不足以补偿\n358\t    variance cost。 Bootstrap CI 包含 0，说明差异 not significant——但 point estimate 方向一致地不利于\n359\t    EC-HTE。审稿人会问 ''if EC-HTE doesn''t help on real data, what''s the practical value?''\n360\t    Worst 档叙事：承认 real data limitation，frame as ''the diagnostic criterion correctly\n361\t    predicts this is a setting where global suffices (Δπ only 0.10)''——但这与 diagnostic\n362\t    CV AUC < 0.55 矛盾，所以叙事需要更 nuanced handling。\n363\t\n364\t    '\n365\t  tables:\n366\t  - title: 'Table 6: Real-data CATE estimates by subgroup and method'\n367\t    columns:\n368\t    - subgroup\n369\t    - n\n370\t    - misclass_rate\n371\t    - naive_cate\n372\t    - global_cate\n373\t    - ec_hte_cate\n374\t    - ec_hte_ci_width\n375\t    representative_rows:\n376\t    - - plat0_long\n377\t      - 624\n378\t      - 0.27\n379\t      - 0.15\n380\t      - 0.19\n381\t      - 0.22\n382\t      - 0.38\n383\t    - - plat0_short\n384\t      - 624\n385\t      - 0.34\n386\t      - 0.08\n387\t      - 0.12\n388\t      - 0.09\n389\t      - 0.41\n390\t    - - plat23_long\n391\t      - 624\n392\t      - 0.3\n393\t      - -0.05\n394\t      - -0.08\n395\t      - -0.12\n396\t      - 0.32\n397\t    - - plat23_short\n398\t      - 624\n399\t      - 0.38\n400\t      - 0.02\n401\t      - 0.05\n402\t      - 0.03\n403\t      - 0.36\n404\t  figures_description:\n405\t  - 'Forest plot: CATE ± CI for each subgroup × method. EC-HTE CIs visually wider,\n406\t    point estimates sometimes farther from domain expectation.'\n407\t  analysis: 'Real data 结果是 worst 档叙事的最大挑战。EC-HTE 不仅未改善，反而略差。但可以 salvage：(1) 没有 ground\n408\t    truth CATE，''worse'' 仅指 point estimate 更极端 + wider CI； (2) Δπ=0.10 处于 diagnostic\n409\t    的 ''global suffices'' 区域；(3) 高 FNR 是 dataset-specific limitation。论文可以诚实呈现为 ''EC-HTE\n410\t    is not universally beneficial — consistent with our theoretical analysis showing\n411\t    conditional advantage''。但审稿人仍可能视为 disqualifying。\n412\t\n413\t    '\n414\t- name: Diagnostic criterion validation (CV)\n415\t  plan_id: exp-005\n416\t  description: 'Δπ×Δτ product 作为 diagnostic 预测 global correction failure 的 ROC 分析。\n417\t    Worst 档下 CV AUC 崩塌至 ~0.50，无预测力。\n418\t\n419\t    '\n420\t  expected_results:\n421\t    in_sample_auc: 0.82\n422\t    cv_auc_leave_one_setting_out: 0.52\n423\t    cv_auc_held_out: 0.48\n424\t    subgroup_level_auc_cv: 0.54\n425\t    setting_level_auc_cv: 0.45\n426\t    correlation_product_vs_bias_amplification: 0.4\n427\t    optimal_threshold_in_sample: 0.025\n428\t    threshold_sensitivity: AUC drops from 0.82 to 0.52 when evaluated out-of-sample\n429\t  result_rationale: 'Worst 档核心假设：diagnostic_auc_cv 在 [0.4, 0.55]。In-sample AUC 看起来不错\n430\t    (~0.82），但 leave-one-setting-out CV 暴露了 overfitting：product Δπ×Δτ 的 threshold 在不同\n431\t    DGP/配置间不 transferable。原因：(1) bias amplification 不仅取决于 Δπ×Δτ， 还取决于 n_expert, K,\n432\t    estimator type, subgroup size balance 等未建模因素；(2) 实验配置数量有限（~20-30 settings），leave-one-out\n433\t    每次 test set 只有一个点； (3) product form 是 population-level identity，但 ''when does\n434\t    it matter enough to switch methods'' 是一个 decision problem，需要考虑 variance tradeoff，product\n435\t    form alone 不够。CV AUC ~0.50 意味着 diagnostic 本质上是 random guessing for new settings。\n436\t    审稿人会直接否定 Claim 3。\n437\t\n438\t    '\n439\t  tables:\n440\t  - title: 'Table 7: Diagnostic ROC analysis'\n441\t    columns:\n442\t    - evaluation\n443\t    - auc\n444\t    - 95_ci\n445\t    - n_settings\n446\t    representative_rows:\n447\t    - - in_sample\n448\t      - 0.82\n449\t      - '[0.74, 0.90]'\n450\t      - 28\n451\t    - - leave_one_setting_out\n452\t      - 0.52\n453\t      - '[0.38, 0.66]'\n454\t      - 28\n455\t    - - held_out_semi_synthetic\n456\t      - 0.48\n457\t      - '[0.30, 0.66]'\n458\t      - 12\n459\t  figures_description:\n460\t  - 'ROC curves: in-sample（实线，AUC=0.82）vs CV（虚线，AUC=0.52）。CV 曲线几乎贴着 diagonal。'\n461\t  analysis: 'Diagnostic CV failure 是 worst 档的 defining feature。In-sample vs CV gap\n462\t    巨大， 说明 Δπ×Δτ product 虽然在 population level 是精确 identity，但作为 finite-sample decision\n463\t    rule 不泛化。Worst 档叙事：放弃 diagnostic 作为 ''decision tool''，重构为 ''sufficient condition\n464\t    for concern''——当 Δπ×Δτ 非常大时，global correction 肯定有风险 （这是 identity 的直接推论），但 intermediate\n465\t    values 无法可靠区分。这实际上是从 Claim 3 退回到 Claim 1 的推论。\n466\t\n467\t    '\n468\t- name: Expert label budget sensitivity\n469\t  plan_id: exp-006\n470\t  description: 'n_expert × K × regime 的系统性 sweep，找 EC-HTE > Global 的 crossover point。\n471\t    Worst 档下 crossover 要求大量 expert labels，moderate regime 永远不 cross。\n472\t\n473\t    '\n474\t  expected_results:\n475\t    n_mc: 100\n476\t    grid: n_expert=[50,100,250,500,1000,2000] × K=[2,4,8] × regime=[extreme,moderate]\n477\t    crossover_hb_beats_global:\n478\t      K2_extreme: 500\n479\t      K2_moderate: never\n480\t      K4_extreme: 2000\n481\t      K4_moderate: never\n482\t      K8_extreme: never\n483\t      K8_moderate: never\n484\t    hb_vs_mle_pct_configs_hb_wins: 60%\n485\t    hb_vs_mle_max_improvement: +15% RMSE (K4/moderate/n50)\n486\t    ec_hte_rmse_penalty_median: 1.6\n487\t    ec_hte_rmse_penalty_k4_n100: 2.3\n488\t    ec_hte_rmse_penalty_k8_n100: 3.5\n489\t  result_rationale: 'Worst 档假设 ec_hte_rmse_penalty_median 在 [1.3, 2.5]，hb_crossover_k4_moderate\n490\t    = [2000, never]。Crossover points 全面上移：K=2/extreme 从 250 升到 500（需要 双倍 expert labels），K=4/extreme\n491\t    从 1000 升到 2000（接近 impractical），K=4/moderate 和所有 K=8 配置永远不 cross。原因：worst 档下 EC-HTE\n492\t    的 bias 优势本身较弱 （reduction factor 仅 0.8-1.5×），RMSE penalty 更重（per-subgroup CM estimation\n493\t    noise 高），两者叠加导致 crossover 需要更多 data 来 amortize variance cost。 K=8 是 worst 档新增的\n494\t    stress test——8 subgroups 意味着 n_expert/8 极少，CM 估计 完全不可靠。审稿人会指出 ''crossover requires\n495\t    2000 expert labels for K=4 — at that point, why not just use expert labels directly\n496\t    for CATE?''\n497\t\n498\t    '\n499\t  tables:\n500\t  - title: 'Table 8: RMSE crossover n_expert by K × regime'\n501\t    columns:\n502\t    - K\n503\t    - regime\n504\t    - crossover_n\n505\t    - ec_hte_rmse_at_crossover\n506\t    - global_rmse_at_crossover\n507\t    representative_rows:\n508\t    - - 2\n509\t      - extreme\n510\t      - 500\n511\t      - 0.13\n512\t      - 0.132\n513\t    - - 2\n514\t      - moderate\n515\t      - never\n516\t      - —\n517\t      - —\n518\t    - - 4\n519\t      - extreme\n520\t      - 2000\n521\t      - 0.088\n522\t      - 0.09\n523\t    - - 4\n524\t      - moderate\n525\t      - never\n526\t      - —\n527\t      - —\n528\t    - - 8\n529\t      - extreme\n530\t      - never\n531\t      - —\n532\t      - —\n533\t    - - 8\n534\t      - moderate\n535\t      - never\n536\t      - —\n537\t      - —\n538\t  figures_description:\n539\t  - 'Line plot: RMSE vs n_expert for each K, with global as horizontal reference line.\n540\t    EC-HTE curves slowly approach global from above; only K=2/extreme and K=4/extreme\n541\t    eventually cross.'\n542\t  analysis: 'Budget analysis 彻底暴露 EC-HTE 的 practical limitation：在多数现实场景（moderate heterogeneity\n543\t    或 K>4），global correction 始终是更好的选择。EC-HTE 唯一有价值的 scenario 是 extreme heterogeneity\n544\t    + small K + large expert budget——这是一个非常 narrow niche。论文必须 honestly present 这些\n545\t    crossover，强化 ''conditional advantage'' framing。审稿人会用 K=8/never 结果论证 EC-HTE 缺乏\n546\t    scalability。\n547\t\n548\t    '\n549\t- name: PPCI + DSL baseline comparison\n550\t  plan_id: exp-007\n551\t  description: 'PPCI vs EC-HTE vs DSL 在四种 DGP 下的比较。Worst 档下 PPCI 在 DGP A (covariate-only\n552\t    error) 也有 partial correction 能力，削弱 EC-HTE 独特性。\n553\t\n554\t    '\n555\t  expected_results:\n556\t    total_configs: 48\n557\t    mc_runs: 100\n558\t    dgp_a_covariate_only:\n559\t      ec_hte_avg_bias: 0.03\n560\t      ec_hte_avg_rmse: 0.18\n561\t      global_avg_bias: 0.08\n562\t      global_avg_rmse: 0.12\n563\t      ppci_avg_bias: 0.05\n564\t      ppci_avg_rmse: 0.14\n565\t      dsl_per_subgroup_avg_bias: 0.04\n566\t      dsl_per_subgroup_avg_rmse: 0.2\n567\t    dgp_b_outcome_only:\n568\t      ec_hte_avg_bias: 0.08\n569\t      ppci_avg_bias: 0.02\n570\t      global_avg_bias: 0.07\n571\t    dgp_c_both_errors:\n572\t      ec_hte_ppci_avg_bias: 0.008\n573\t      ec_hte_avg_bias: 0.15\n574\t      ppci_avg_bias: 0.06\n575\t      global_avg_bias: 0.12\n576\t    dgp_d_no_error:\n577\t      all_methods_bias: <0.01\n578\t    ec_hte_unique_advantage_over_ppci_dgp_a: bias 0.03 vs 0.05 (40% better, but RMSE\n579\t      29% worse)\n580\t    ppci_partial_covariate_correction: true\n581\t  result_rationale: 'Worst 档下 PPCI 在 DGP A（纯 covariate error）也能 partially correct（bias\n582\t    0.05 vs EC-HTE 0.03）——因为 PPCI rectifier 是 model-free，可以捕获任何 systematic error 包括\n583\t    covariate-side。这削弱了 ''EC-HTE is uniquely needed for covariate error'' 的 论点。EC-HTE\n584\t    仍然 slightly better on bias（0.03 vs 0.05），但 RMSE penalty 使得 net advantage ambiguous。DSL\n585\t    per-subgroup 的 bias 与 EC-HTE comparable（0.04 vs 0.03），验证了审稿人的担忧：''just apply DSL\n586\t    per subgroup, no need for HB''。DGP C 的 composition 仍然有效（ec_hte_ppci bias 0.008），但审稿人会指出\n587\t    PPCI alone 已经 做到 0.06——composition 的 marginal gain 可能不值得复杂度。\n588\t\n589\t    '\n590\t  tables:\n591\t  - title: 'Table 9: Method comparison across DGP types (n_expert=250, K=2, extreme)'\n592\t    columns:\n593\t    - dgp\n594\t    - method\n595\t    - avg_abs_bias\n596\t    - avg_rmse\n597\t    - coverage\n598\t    representative_rows:\n599\t    - - A\n600\t      - ec_hte\n601\t      - 0.03\n602\t      - 0.18\n603\t      - 0.93\n604\t    - - A\n605\t      - ppci\n606\t      - 0.05\n607\t      - 0.14\n608\t      - 0.9\n609\t    - - A\n610\t      - dsl_subgroup\n611\t      - 0.04\n612\t      - 0.2\n613\t      - 0.88\n614\t    - - A\n615\t      - global\n616\t      - 0.08\n617\t      - 0.12\n618\t      - 0.82\n619\t    - - B\n620\t      - ec_hte\n621\t      - 0.08\n622\t      - 0.16\n623\t      - 0.9\n624\t    - - B\n625\t      - ppci\n626\t      - 0.02\n627\t      - 0.13\n628\t      - 0.94\n629\t    - - C\n630\t      - ec_hte_ppci\n631\t      - 0.008\n632\t      - 0.2\n633\t      - 0.95\n634\t    - - C\n635\t      - ppci\n636\t      - 0.06\n637\t      - 0.14\n638\t      - 0.91\n639\t    - - C\n640\t      - ec_hte\n641\t      - 0.15\n642\t      - 0.19\n643\t      - 0.88\n644\t  figures_description:\n645\t  - 'Grouped bar chart: |bias| by DGP × method. EC-HTE 优势仅在 DGP A 可见且 modest；PPCI\n646\t    在所有 DGP 都 reasonable。'\n647\t  analysis: 'PPCI 的 partial covariate correction 是 worst 档的关键 negative signal——如果一个\n648\t    通用方法已经能 partially correct covariate error，EC-HTE 的 ''structured correction for\n649\t    covariate error'' 卖点被显著削弱。DSL per-subgroup 作为 simple baseline 表现 surprisingly\n650\t    close to EC-HTE，进一步降低 novelty argument。Composition 仍然 works but marginal gain\n651\t    over PPCI alone 有限。论文需要诚实承认 PPCI 的 partial coverage 并 reframe EC-HTE 的价值为 ''structured\n652\t    + interpretable'' 而非 ''strictly necessary''。\n653\t\n654\t    '\n655\t- name: Multiple LLM annotator comparison\n656\t  plan_id: exp-008\n657\t  description: '多 LLM 比较 misclassification heterogeneity patterns。Worst 档下 heterogeneity\n658\t    存在但 Δπ 较小，EC-HTE benefit 因此更弱。\n659\t\n660\t    '\n661\t  expected_results:\n662\t    models_completed:\n663\t    - gpt-3.5-turbo\n664\t    - gpt-4.1\n665\t    - gpt-4o\n666\t    - gpt-4o-mini\n667\t    - gpt-4-turbo\n668\t    - gpt-5.4\n669\t    effective_delta_pi:\n670\t      gpt-3.5-turbo: 0.15\n671\t      gpt-4-turbo: 0.1\n672\t      gpt-4.1: 0.06\n673\t      gpt-4o: 0.05\n674\t      gpt-4o-mini: 0.09\n675\t      gpt-5.4: 0.05\n676\t    all_delta_pi_above_005: true\n677\t    median_delta_pi: 0.075\n678\t    ec_hte_benefit_prediction: At median Δπ=0.075, expected bias amplification ~1.15×\n679\t      — minimal practical impact\n680\t    worst_subgroup_consensus: True_medium (4/6 models)\n681\t    newer_models_lower_delta_pi: true\n682\t  result_rationale: '所有 LLM 都展示 Δπ > 0.05（heterogeneity 是 structural），但 newer/better\n683\t    models （GPT-4o, GPT-5.4）的 Δπ 更低（~0.05）。这意味着随着 LLM 进步，misclassification heterogeneity\n684\t    自然减小，EC-HTE 的 relevance 随之递减。Worst 档叙事：''EC-HTE solves a problem that is diminishing\n685\t    as LLMs improve''。Median Δπ=0.075 对应的 bias amplification 仅 ~1.15×——审稿人会问 ''is\n686\t    15% amplification worth the complexity of HB correction?''。论文可以 salvage by arguing\n687\t    that even 5% heterogeneity exists and Claim 1 formal characterization remains\n688\t    relevant——但 EC-HTE 的实际价值主张被 削弱。\n689\t\n690\t    '\n691\t  tables:\n692\t  - title: 'Table 10: Δπ by LLM model generation'\n693\t    columns:\n694\t    - model\n695\t    - generation\n696\t    - accuracy\n697\t    - delta_pi\n698\t    - predicted_max_amplification\n699\t    representative_rows:\n700\t    - - gpt-3.5-turbo\n701\t      - '3.5'\n702\t      - 0.72\n703\t      - 0.15\n704\t      - 1.8×\n705\t    - - gpt-4-turbo\n706\t      - '4'\n707\t      - 0.81\n708\t      - 0.1\n709\t      - 1.4×\n710\t    - - gpt-4.1\n711\t      - '4.1'\n712\t      - 0.86\n713\t      - 0.06\n714\t      - 1.15×\n715\t    - - gpt-5.4\n716\t      - '5'\n717\t      - 0.9\n718\t      - 0.05\n719\t      - 1.10×\n720\t  figures_description:\n721\t  - 'Line plot: Δπ vs model generation/accuracy. 下降趋势明显——better models → less heterogeneity。'\n722\t  analysis: 'Multi-LLM 结果是 double-edged：确认 heterogeneity 是 universal（所有 LLM 都有）， 但也确认它在\n723\t    diminishing。审稿人可能用 GPT-5.4 的 Δπ=0.05 论证 ''the problem is already mostly solved\n724\t    by better models''。论文可以 counter：(1) 即使 Δπ=0.05， 在 high-stakes CSS 中 any bias matters；(2)\n725\t    less-capable models 仍广泛使用 （cost reasons）；(3) Claim 1 的 formal characterization\n726\t    不取决于 Δπ 大小。\n727\t\n728\t    '\n729\t- name: Adaptive expert annotation allocation\n730\t  plan_id: exp-009\n731\t  description: 'CATE-weighted allocation vs uniform vs uncertainty-only。Worst 档下 adaptive\n732\t    allocation 的改进 negligible。\n733\t\n734\t    '\n735\t  expected_results:\n736\t    allocation_strategies:\n737\t    - uniform\n738\t    - uncertainty_only\n739\t    - cate_weighted\n740\t    - oracle_allocation\n741\t    n_expert: 250\n742\t    K: 4\n743\t    regime: extreme\n744\t    avg_rmse:\n745\t      uniform: 0.175\n746\t      uncertainty_only: 0.17\n747\t      cate_weighted: 0.168\n748\t      oracle_allocation: 0.155\n749\t    avg_bias:\n750\t      uniform: 0.065\n751\t      uncertainty_only: 0.06\n752\t      cate_weighted: 0.058\n753\t      oracle_allocation: 0.045\n754\t    cate_weighted_vs_uniform_rmse_improvement: 4%\n755\t    cate_weighted_vs_uniform_bias_improvement: 11%\n756\t  result_rationale: 'Worst 档下 EC-HTE 本身优势微弱，adaptive allocation 在此基础上进一步优化的空间 很小。CATE-weighted\n757\t    vs uniform 仅 4% RMSE 改进和 11% bias 改进——统计上可能不 significant。原因：(1) 当 EC-HTE 的 bias\n758\t    reduction 本身就 modest 时，optimally allocating labels 的 marginal return 也 modest；(2)\n759\t    CATE heterogeneity 未知（需要 initial estimate），estimation error 吃掉了 allocation gain；(3)\n760\t    K=4 时 subgroup sizes unbalanced，minority subgroups 已经需要所有能得到的 labels，allocation\n761\t    灵活性 有限。P2 priority 合理——这个实验在 worst 档下几乎无论文价值。\n762\t\n763\t    '\n764\t  tables:\n765\t  - title: 'Table 11: Allocation strategy comparison (K=4, extreme, n=250)'\n766\t    columns:\n767\t    - strategy\n768\t    - avg_bias\n769\t    - avg_rmse\n770\t    - worst_subgroup_rmse\n771\t    representative_rows:\n772\t    - - uniform\n773\t      - 0.065\n774\t      - 0.175\n775\t      - 0.28\n776\t    - - uncertainty_only\n777\t      - 0.06\n778\t      - 0.17\n779\t      - 0.26\n780\t    - - cate_weighted\n781\t      - 0.058\n782\t      - 0.168\n783\t      - 0.25\n784\t    - - oracle\n785\t      - 0.045\n786\t      - 0.155\n787\t      - 0.2\n788\t  figures_description:\n789\t  - 'Bar chart: RMSE by allocation strategy. 差异非常小，error bars 重叠。'\n790\t  analysis: 'Adaptive allocation 在 worst 档下是 noise。Improvement 太小，不值得 paper space。\n791\t    在 reframed 单 claim 论文中完全删除。\n792\t\n793\t    '\n794\t- name: Robustness to misspecified subgroup structure\n795\t  plan_id: exp-010\n796\t  description: 'EC-HTE 在 subgroup 定义 noisy/misspecified 时的表现。Worst 档下 EC-HTE 对 misspecification\n797\t    敏感。\n798\t\n799\t    '\n800\t  expected_results:\n801\t    noise_levels:\n802\t    - 0\n803\t    - 0.1\n804\t    - 0.25\n805\t    - 0.5\n806\t    K2_ec_hte_rmse:\n807\t    - 0.16\n808\t    - 0.17\n809\t    - 0.19\n810\t    - 0.22\n811\t    K2_global_rmse:\n812\t    - 0.12\n813\t    - 0.12\n814\t    - 0.12\n815\t    - 0.12\n816\t    K4_ec_hte_rmse:\n817\t    - 0.2\n818\t    - 0.22\n819\t    - 0.26\n820\t    - 0.3\n821\t    K4_global_rmse:\n822\t    - 0.14\n823\t    - 0.14\n824\t    - 0.14\n825\t    - 0.14\n826\t    K2_ec_hte_coverage:\n827\t    - 0.93\n828\t    - 0.91\n829\t    - 0.88\n830\t    - 0.86\n831\t    K4_ec_hte_coverage:\n832\t    - 0.92\n833\t    - 0.89\n834\t    - 0.85\n835\t    - 0.82\n836\t    graceful_convergence_at_50pct: false\n837\t    ec_hte_worse_than_global_at_noise_25pct: true\n838\t  result_rationale: 'Worst 档假设 coverage_ec_hte_small_n 在 [0.85, 0.92]。当 subgroup assignment\n839\t    有 noise 时，per-subgroup CM 估计受污染，EC-HTE 的 stratification 变成 liability。 Global correction\n840\t    对 subgroup noise immune（它本来就不 condition on subgroups）。 在 25% noise level，EC-HTE\n841\t    的 RMSE 已经显著劣于 global（K=4: 0.26 vs 0.14）， coverage 跌到 0.85。HB shrinkage 理论上应该 gracefully\n842\t    degrade 但在 worst 档下 concentration prior 不够 strong 来 pull noisy subgroups back\n843\t    to global。这比 actual exp-010 结果（coverage 0.946 at 50% noise）显著差——worst 档假设 HB 实现或\n844\t    prior calibration 有问题。审稿人会用这个结果论证 EC-HTE 在 real settings（subgroups never perfectly\n845\t    known）不可靠。\n846\t\n847\t    '\n848\t  tables:\n849\t  - title: 'Table 12: Robustness to subgroup misspecification (K=4, n_expert=250)'\n850\t    columns:\n851\t    - noise_level\n852\t    - ec_hte_rmse\n853\t    - global_rmse\n854\t    - ec_hte_coverage\n855\t    - penalty_ratio\n856\t    representative_rows:\n857\t    - - 0.0\n858\t      - 0.2\n859\t      - 0.14\n860\t      - 0.92\n861\t      - 1.43\n862\t    - - 0.1\n863\t      - 0.22\n864\t      - 0.14\n865\t      - 0.89\n866\t      - 1.57\n867\t    - - 0.25\n868\t      - 0.26\n869\t      - 0.14\n870\t      - 0.85\n871\t      - 1.86\n872\t    - - 0.5\n873\t      - 0.3\n874\t      - 0.14\n875\t      - 0.82\n876\t      - 2.14\n877\t  figures_description:\n878\t  - 'Line plot: RMSE vs noise level for EC-HTE vs global. EC-HTE 斜率陡峭上升，global 平坦。'\n879\t  analysis: 'Robustness results 在 worst 档下是 EC-HTE 的又一 liability。Real-world subgroup\n880\t    definitions 不会是 noise-free，25% misspecification 是 conservative estimate。 EC-HTE\n881\t    的 penalty ratio 从 1.43 增加到 2.14——比 clean 条件下更差。这进一步 限制了 EC-HTE 的 practical applicability。论文需要非常\n882\t    honest 地报告这些结果 并明确 ''EC-HTE requires well-defined subgroups'' 作为 limitation。\n883\t\n884\t    '\n885\t- name: Causal forest integration\n886\t  plan_id: exp-011\n887\t  description: 'CausalForestDML + EC-HTE post-hoc correction。Worst 档下 causal forest\n888\t    放大了 debiasing-hurts effect（支持 Claim 1），但 EC-HTE correction 的 RMSE penalty 更严重。\n889\t\n890\t    '\n891\t  expected_results:\n892\t    n_mc: 100\n893\t    n_configs: 8\n894\t    mean_abs_bias:\n895\t      naive_forest: 0.16\n896\t      global_forest: 0.12\n897\t      ec_hte_forest: 0.08\n898\t    mean_rmse:\n899\t      naive_forest: 0.18\n900\t      global_forest: 0.17\n901\t      ec_hte_forest: 0.28\n902\t    debiasing_hurts_cases: 10\n903\t    debiasing_hurts_max_ratio: 5.2\n904\t    ec_hte_rmse_penalty_vs_global: 1.65\n905\t    ec_hte_forest_coverage: 0.88\n906\t    bias_reduction_factor: 1.5\n907\t  result_rationale: 'Causal forest 放大了 bias mechanism（max ratio 5.2×，因为 tree-based\n908\t    CATE 的 nonlinear estimation 在 subgroup boundaries 处 compounds error），强力支持 Claim\n909\t    1。 但同时 EC-HTE correction 的 RMSE penalty 更重（1.65× vs global），因为 forest pseudo-outcomes\n910\t    已经 noisy，再加上 per-subgroup CM correction noise 叠加。 Coverage 0.88 低于 nominal 95%——forest\n911\t    variance estimation 加 CM uncertainty 的 joint calibration 有问题。Bias reduction factor\n912\t    1.5× 处于 worst 档上限—— EC-HTE 确实 helps on bias 但代价高。这进一步支持 ''reframe around Claim\n913\t    1'' 叙事： CausalForest 使得 debiasing-hurts 更 dramatic（5.2× amplification），但 EC-HTE\n914\t    fix 的 cost 也更高。\n915\t\n916\t    '\n917\t  tables:\n918\t  - title: 'Table 13: CausalForest results by K × regime'\n919\t    columns:\n920\t    - K\n921\t    - regime\n922\t    - method\n923\t    - avg_abs_bias\n924\t    - avg_rmse\n925\t    - debiasing_hurts_max_ratio\n926\t    representative_rows:\n927\t    - - 2\n928\t      - extreme\n929\t      - naive_forest\n930\t      - 0.14\n931\t      - 0.17\n932\t      - —\n933\t    - - 2\n934\t      - extreme\n935\t      - global_forest\n936\t      - 0.1\n937\t      - 0.16\n938\t      - 2.8\n939\t    - - 2\n940\t      - extreme\n941\t      - ec_hte_forest\n942\t      - 0.05\n943\t      - 0.24\n944\t      - —\n945\t    - - 4\n946\t      - extreme\n947\t      - naive_forest\n948\t      - 0.18\n949\t      - 0.2\n950\t      - —\n951\t    - - 4\n952\t      - extreme\n953\t      - global_forest\n954\t      - 0.15\n955\t      - 0.18\n956\t      - 5.2\n957\t    - - 4\n958\t      - extreme\n959\t      - ec_hte_forest\n960\t      - 0.09\n961\t      - 0.32\n962\t      - —\n963\t  figures_description:\n964\t  - 'Heatmap: debiasing-hurts ratio by K × subgroup for CausalForest. K=4/extreme/sg0\n965\t    达到 5.2×。'\n966\t  - 'Bias-RMSE scatter: CausalForest methods. EC-HTE 在 bias 轴更好但 RMSE 轴显著更差。'\n967\t  analysis: CausalForest 结果为 Claim 1 提供最强支持——5.2× amplification 是 dramatic 且 practically\n968\t    concerning。但 EC-HTE 的 RMSE penalty (1.65×) 和 undercoverage (0.88) 使得 'the fix\n969\t    is worse than the disease' argument 更 plausible。Worst 档叙事： 'We identify a severe\n970\t    bias mechanism (up to 5.2× with causal forests), but acknowledge that current\n971\t    correction methods trade bias for variance in ways that may not be practically\n972\t    acceptable.' 这支持 reframe 为 negative result paper。\n973\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e9b4a18b-c633-4311-adcc-ec67e4792244","uuid":"c9c00632-8ff9-401a-92a5-177c58715a6b","timestamp":"2026-05-21T13:08:37.770Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0520/projects/ec_hte_llm_annotation/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260521T122454/worst/review_context.yaml","content":"narrative_guidance: '放弃三 Claim 结构，重构为单 claim 论文：''Debiasing Can Hurt — When Global\n  Misclassification Correction Amplifies Subgroup CATE Bias''。Claim 1（bias identity\n  + exact product form + constructive debiasing-hurts proposition）是唯一可靠的核心贡献。EC-HTE\n  降级为 ''one possible mitigation''，诚实承认其优势条件极窄（仅 synthetic extreme + large n_expert）。诊断准则\n  CV AUC 崩塌，重构为 sufficient condition for concern 而非 decision tool。Real data 反向结果不掩盖，\n  作为 ''honest empirical assessment'' 呈现。论文变短、更聚焦、理论更强。投 EMNLP main，定位为 negative result\n  + formal characterization 类型论文。预期需要 2R 或 resubmit。\n\n  '\nimagined_experiments:\n- name: Hierarchical Bayesian EC-HTE synthetic validation\n  plan_id: exp-001\n  description: 'HB Dirichlet-prior confusion matrix estimator vs MLE/Laplace，full\n    regime sweep。 Worst 档下 HB 改进微弱，RMSE penalty 显著，partial pooling 在多数配置无实质优势。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    mcmc_rhat_max: 1.03\n    mcmc_ess_min: 110\n    mcmc_divergent: 0\n    runtime_min: 85\n    total_mc_runs: 3600\n    hb_vs_mle_rmse_improvement_k2_n50: 1-3%\n    hb_vs_mle_rmse_improvement_k2_n100: <1%\n    hb_vs_mle_rmse_improvement_k4_n50_moderate: 2-4%\n    hb_coverage_min: 0.85\n    hb_coverage_median: 0.9\n    k4_extreme_n50_blowup: true\n    k4_extreme_n50_blowup_note: Singularity guard triggers frequently (~15% of runs);\n      residual instability even with 4-chain MCMC\n    hb_vs_global_rmse_median_penalty: 1.5\n    hb_beats_global_pct: 35% of configs (only extreme regime + n>=500)\n    hyperprior_sensitivity_k4_rmse_variation: 8-12%\n    hyperprior_sensitivity_conclusion: moderate sensitivity — k4 results shift meaningfully\n      with scale\n  result_rationale: 'Worst 档核心假设是 EC-HTE 优势微弱。HB partial pooling 在 moderate regime\n    几乎无 改进（heterogeneity 不足以让 stratification 获益），extreme regime 仅在 n_expert 足够大时才有意义。K=4\n    时 per-subgroup 样本太少（n_expert/4），CM 估计噪声高，HB shrinkage 不足以补偿。MCMC 收敛勉强合格但 ESS 偏低，说明后验几何复杂。Hyperprior\n    sensitivity 在 K=4 时较高，因为 Dirichlet concentration 对稀疏子群影响大。整体结论： HB 是一个 marginal\n    improvement over MLE，不构成独立贡献。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Table 1: HB vs MLE vs Global RMSE across regime × K × n_expert'\n    columns:\n    - regime\n    - K\n    - n_expert\n    - naive_rmse\n    - global_rmse\n    - mle_rmse\n    - hb_rmse\n    - hb_vs_global_pct\n    representative_rows:\n    - - extreme\n      - 2\n      - 100\n      - 0.18\n      - 0.15\n      - 0.17\n      - 0.16\n      - +6.7%\n    - - extreme\n      - 2\n      - 500\n      - 0.18\n      - 0.15\n      - 0.13\n      - 0.13\n      - -13.3%\n    - - extreme\n      - 4\n      - 100\n      - 0.2\n      - 0.16\n      - 0.25\n      - 0.23\n      - +43.8%\n    - - extreme\n      - 4\n      - 500\n      - 0.2\n      - 0.16\n      - 0.16\n      - 0.15\n      - -6.3%\n    - - moderate\n      - 2\n      - 100\n      - 0.14\n      - 0.12\n      - 0.13\n      - 0.13\n      - +8.3%\n    - - moderate\n      - 2\n      - 500\n      - 0.14\n      - 0.12\n      - 0.12\n      - 0.12\n      - 0%\n    - - moderate\n      - 4\n      - 100\n      - 0.16\n      - 0.13\n      - 0.19\n      - 0.18\n      - +38.5%\n    - - moderate\n      - 4\n      - 500\n      - 0.16\n      - 0.13\n      - 0.14\n      - 0.13\n      - 0%\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Heatmap: HB vs Global RMSE ratio across n_expert × K grid. 大面积 >1.0（红色），仅右下角（high\n    n, extreme）<1.0（蓝色）'\n  analysis: 'EC-HTE 在多数实际配置下 RMSE 劣于 global。Partial pooling 的 James-Stein 优势 被 per-subgroup\n    CM 估计噪声淹没。仅在 extreme heterogeneity + n_expert >= 500 时 才有 RMSE 优势。这决定了 worst 档叙事：EC-HTE\n    不能作为 standalone contribution， 只能作为 conditional mitigation 附在 bias mechanism 主线之后。\n\n    '\n- name: Formal bias identity verification\n  plan_id: exp-002\n  description: 'Bias = Δπ × Δτ product form 的 analytic derivation + MC 验证。Worst 档下\n    identity 本身成立（这是数学事实），但 amplification magnitude 处于范围低端。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    r2_k2: 0.99\n    r2_k4: 0.965\n    tightness_ratio_k2_median: 1.005\n    tightness_ratio_k4_median: 1.035\n    debiasing_hurts_pct: 48\n    debiasing_hurts_pct_note: 略低于 50%，因为 MC noise 在 boundary 附近导致一些 marginal cases\n      翻转\n    max_bias_ratio_k2: 2.5\n    max_bias_ratio_k4: 2.4\n    coverage_2se_k2: 0.945\n    coverage_2se_k4: 0.93\n    bias_amplification_median_across_configs: 1.4\n  result_rationale: 'Bias identity 是精确等式（population level），R² 接近 1.0 是数学保证，worst 档无法\n    改变这一点。但 worst 档体现在 amplification magnitude 偏低端：K=2 max 2.5×（而非 2.86×），K=4 max\n    2.4×（而非 2.41×）。这是因为 worst 档假设 moderate regime 占更多 权重——当 Δπ 和 Δτ 都不极端时，amplification\n    存在但不dramatic。Debiasing hurts 的 比例约 48%（接近 coin-flip），审稿人可能认为这不足以构成 ''alarming\n    finding''。K=4 的 R² 稍低反映了 sum-of-products form 在有限样本下的噪声放大。关键问题不在于 identity 是否成立（它一定成立），而在于\n    amplification 的实际幅度是否足以让审稿人认为这是 a problem worth solving。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Table 2: Bias amplification ratio across Δπ × Δτ grid (K=2)'\n    columns:\n    - delta_pi\n    - delta_tau\n    - analytic_bias\n    - mc_bias_mean\n    - mc_bias_se\n    - amplification_ratio\n    representative_rows:\n    - - 0.05\n      - 0.1\n      - 0.005\n      - 0.006\n      - 0.002\n      - 1.1\n    - - 0.1\n      - 0.2\n      - 0.02\n      - 0.021\n      - 0.004\n      - 1.4\n    - - 0.15\n      - 0.3\n      - 0.045\n      - 0.046\n      - 0.006\n      - 1.8\n    - - 0.2\n      - 0.5\n      - 0.1\n      - 0.098\n      - 0.008\n      - 2.5\n  - title: 'Table 3: Debiasing-hurts breakdown by parameter region'\n    columns:\n    - region\n    - n_settings\n    - hurts_pct\n    - max_ratio\n    - median_ratio\n    representative_rows:\n    - - extreme (Δπ>0.15, Δτ>0.3)\n      - 40\n      - 85\n      - 2.5\n      - 1.8\n    - - moderate (0.05<Δπ<0.15)\n      - 120\n      - 52\n      - 1.5\n      - 1.1\n    - - low (Δπ<0.05)\n      - 100\n      - 12\n      - 1.05\n      - 1.0\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Heatmap: amplification ratio as function of Δπ × Δτ. 颜色梯度从 1.0（白）到 2.5（深红）。高\n    amplification 区域集中在右上角但面积有限。'\n  - 'Scatter: analytic prediction vs MC observed bias, R²=0.990(K=2) / 0.965(K=4).\n    对角线拟合良好。'\n  analysis: 'Bias identity 验证成功——这是 worst 档唯一完全 robust 的结果。但 amplification 幅度在 moderate\n    regime 仅 1.1-1.5×，审稿人可能认为 ''debiasing hurts by 10-50% is a known risk, not a new\n    discovery''。Worst 档叙事必须强调 extreme regime 的 2.5× amplification 和 constructive example，同时承认\n    moderate regime 的 effect size 较小。 Carroll et al. (2006) 的 qualitative insight\n    已覆盖 ''correction can amplify error'' 的概念；我们的 quantitative product form 是增量贡献而非\n    breakthrough。\n\n    '\n- name: Semi-synthetic benchmark (TweetEval sentiment)\n  plan_id: exp-003\n  description: 'TweetEval sentiment 语料上注入 CATE heterogeneity，GPT-4.1 annotation，EC-HTE\n    vs baselines。Worst 档下 EC-HTE 在 semi-synthetic 上优势微弱，RMSE penalty 大。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    n_subgroups: 4\n    misclass_rates: S0=0.08, S1=0.12, S2=0.14, S3=0.22\n    delta_pi: 0.14\n    mc_runs: 100\n    avg_abs_bias:\n      oracle: 0.005\n      naive: 0.12\n      global_corrected: 0.09\n      stratified_mle: 0.07\n      hb_ec_hte: 0.065\n    avg_rmse:\n      oracle: 0.04\n      naive: 0.15\n      global_corrected: 0.12\n      stratified_mle: 0.18\n      hb_ec_hte: 0.16\n    ec_hte_bias_reduction_vs_global: 1.38\n    ec_hte_rmse_penalty_vs_global: 1.33\n    hb_vs_mle_n100_S3: -5% RMSE (HB slightly worse)\n    hb_vs_mle_n250_S3: +8% RMSE (HB slightly better)\n    coverage_hb_overall: 0.91\n    debiasing_hurts_confirmed: true\n    debiasing_hurts_subgroups: S0, S1 (low-error subgroups over-corrected)\n  result_rationale: 'Worst 档假设 ec_hte_bias_reduction_factor_vs_global 在 [0.8, 1.5]\n    范围。这里取 1.38——EC-HTE 比 global 好 28% 在 bias 上，但 RMSE 代价 33%。Semi-synthetic 的 Δπ=0.14（moderate-to-high），足够让\n    bias mechanism 可见但不足以让 EC-HTE 在 RMSE 上胜出。HB 在 n=100 时对 minority subgroup S3 仍然\n    noisy（12.5 experts/subgroup for K=4），partial pooling 不够补偿。审稿人看到 bias 降了但 RMSE\n    升了，会问 ''is this a net improvement?''——答案在 worst 档下是 ambiguous。Coverage 0.91 勉强\n    acceptable 但不 impressive。关键：debiasing hurts 在 S0/S1 上仍然可见，这支持 Claim 1 叙事。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Table 4: Semi-synthetic results by subgroup (n_expert=250, K=4)'\n    columns:\n    - subgroup\n    - misclass_rate\n    - naive_bias\n    - global_bias\n    - ec_hte_bias\n    - ec_hte_rmse\n    - global_rmse\n    representative_rows:\n    - - S0\n      - 0.08\n      - 0.02\n      - 0.07\n      - 0.03\n      - 0.14\n      - 0.1\n    - - S1\n      - 0.12\n      - 0.05\n      - 0.06\n      - 0.04\n      - 0.13\n      - 0.1\n    - - S2\n      - 0.14\n      - 0.08\n      - 0.04\n      - 0.03\n      - 0.15\n      - 0.11\n    - - S3\n      - 0.22\n      - 0.15\n      - 0.1\n      - 0.06\n      - 0.22\n      - 0.16\n  - title: 'Table 5: Bias-RMSE tradeoff summary across n_expert'\n    columns:\n    - n_expert\n    - ec_hte_wins_bias\n    - ec_hte_wins_rmse\n    - net_ambiguous\n    representative_rows:\n    - - 100\n      - 3/4 subgroups\n      - 0/4 subgroups\n      - 4/4\n    - - 250\n      - 4/4 subgroups\n      - 1/4 subgroups\n      - 3/4\n    - - 500\n      - 4/4 subgroups\n      - 2/4 subgroups\n      - 2/4\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Bar chart: |bias| by method × subgroup. EC-HTE bars consistently shorter but\n    difference modest.'\n  - 'Scatter: bias reduction vs RMSE penalty per config. 多数点在 ''bias better, RMSE\n    worse'' 象限。'\n  analysis: 'Semi-synthetic 结果支持 Claim 1（debiasing hurts 在 S0/S1 可见）但不支持 EC-HTE 作为\n    strong solution。Bias-RMSE tradeoff 在多数配置下 ambiguous——审稿人会引用 ''reduces bias but\n    increases MSE — net negative in practice''。Worst 档叙事：这些 结果 honestly show EC-HTE\n    的条件性优势，论文重心应放在 bias mechanism discovery 而非 EC-HTE method contribution。\n\n    '\n- name: Real-data case study (UC Berkeley Hate Speech)\n  plan_id: exp-004\n  description: 'UC Berkeley Measuring Hate Speech 数据集上的 pattern consistency 分析。Worst\n    档下 EC-HTE 比 global 差——real data 反向。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    dataset: UC Berkeley Measuring Hate Speech\n    n_comments: 2496\n    subgroups: platform_group × text_length (4 groups)\n    delta_pi: 0.1\n    global_FPR: 0.15\n    global_FNR: 0.55\n    avg_abs_bias:\n      naive: 0.22\n      global: 0.28\n      ec_hte: 0.32\n    ec_hte_minus_global_abs_bias: 0.04\n    bootstrap_ci_ec_hte_minus_global: '[-0.02, 0.10]'\n    cate_direction_consistency: 2/4 subgroups consistent with domain knowledge\n    ec_hte_ci_width_median: 0.35\n    global_ci_width_median: 0.22\n  result_rationale: 'Worst 档核心假设之一：real data 持续显示 EC-HTE 比 global 差（|bias| 差距 ~0.04）。\n    原因是多方面的：(1) 高 FNR (~55%) 意味着 confusion matrix 接近 singular，逆矩阵 amplifies estimation\n    noise；(2) 仅 2496 samples 分 4 subgroups，per-subgroup expert labels 不足（~600/group，但\n    CM 估计仍 noisy）；(3) text-feature subgroups 可能不对应 true misclassification heterogeneity\n    structure（misspecified subgroups）； (4) Δπ=0.10 处于 moderate 范围，stratification 收益不足以补偿\n    variance cost。 Bootstrap CI 包含 0，说明差异 not significant——但 point estimate 方向一致地不利于\n    EC-HTE。审稿人会问 ''if EC-HTE doesn''t help on real data, what''s the practical value?''\n    Worst 档叙事：承认 real data limitation，frame as ''the diagnostic criterion correctly\n    predicts this is a setting where global suffices (Δπ only 0.10)''——但这与 diagnostic\n    CV AUC < 0.55 矛盾，所以叙事需要更 nuanced handling。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Table 6: Real-data CATE estimates by subgroup and method'\n    columns:\n    - subgroup\n    - n\n    - misclass_rate\n    - naive_cate\n    - global_cate\n    - ec_hte_cate\n    - ec_hte_ci_width\n    representative_rows:\n    - - plat0_long\n      - 624\n      - 0.27\n      - 0.15\n      - 0.19\n      - 0.22\n      - 0.38\n    - - plat0_short\n      - 624\n      - 0.34\n      - 0.08\n      - 0.12\n      - 0.09\n      - 0.41\n    - - plat23_long\n      - 624\n      - 0.3\n      - -0.05\n      - -0.08\n      - -0.12\n      - 0.32\n    - - plat23_short\n      - 624\n      - 0.38\n      - 0.02\n      - 0.05\n      - 0.03\n      - 0.36\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Forest plot: CATE ± CI for each subgroup × method. EC-HTE CIs visually wider,\n    point estimates sometimes farther from domain expectation.'\n  analysis: 'Real data 结果是 worst 档叙事的最大挑战。EC-HTE 不仅未改善，反而略差。但可以 salvage：(1) 没有 ground\n    truth CATE，''worse'' 仅指 point estimate 更极端 + wider CI； (2) Δπ=0.10 处于 diagnostic\n    的 ''global suffices'' 区域；(3) 高 FNR 是 dataset-specific limitation。论文可以诚实呈现为 ''EC-HTE\n    is not universally beneficial — consistent with our theoretical analysis showing\n    conditional advantage''。但审稿人仍可能视为 disqualifying。\n\n    '\n- name: Diagnostic criterion validation (CV)\n  plan_id: exp-005\n  description: 'Δπ×Δτ product 作为 diagnostic 预测 global correction failure 的 ROC 分析。\n    Worst 档下 CV AUC 崩塌至 ~0.50，无预测力。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    in_sample_auc: 0.82\n    cv_auc_leave_one_setting_out: 0.52\n    cv_auc_held_out: 0.48\n    subgroup_level_auc_cv: 0.54\n    setting_level_auc_cv: 0.45\n    correlation_product_vs_bias_amplification: 0.4\n    optimal_threshold_in_sample: 0.025\n    threshold_sensitivity: AUC drops from 0.82 to 0.52 when evaluated out-of-sample\n  result_rationale: 'Worst 档核心假设：diagnostic_auc_cv 在 [0.4, 0.55]。In-sample AUC 看起来不错\n    (~0.82），但 leave-one-setting-out CV 暴露了 overfitting：product Δπ×Δτ 的 threshold 在不同\n    DGP/配置间不 transferable。原因：(1) bias amplification 不仅取决于 Δπ×Δτ， 还取决于 n_expert, K,\n    estimator type, subgroup size balance 等未建模因素；(2) 实验配置数量有限（~20-30 settings），leave-one-out\n    每次 test set 只有一个点； (3) product form 是 population-level identity，但 ''when does\n    it matter enough to switch methods'' 是一个 decision problem，需要考虑 variance tradeoff，product\n    form alone 不够。CV AUC ~0.50 意味着 diagnostic 本质上是 random guessing for new settings。\n    审稿人会直接否定 Claim 3。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Table 7: Diagnostic ROC analysis'\n    columns:\n    - evaluation\n    - auc\n    - 95_ci\n    - n_settings\n    representative_rows:\n    - - in_sample\n      - 0.82\n      - '[0.74, 0.90]'\n      - 28\n    - - leave_one_setting_out\n      - 0.52\n      - '[0.38, 0.66]'\n      - 28\n    - - held_out_semi_synthetic\n      - 0.48\n      - '[0.30, 0.66]'\n      - 12\n  figures_description:\n  - 'ROC curves: in-sample（实线，AUC=0.82）vs CV（虚线，AUC=0.52）。CV 曲线几乎贴着 diagonal。'\n  analysis: 'Diagnostic CV failure 是 worst 档的 defining feature。In-sample vs CV gap\n    巨大， 说明 Δπ×Δτ product 虽然在 population level 是精确 identity，但作为 finite-sample decision\n    rule 不泛化。Worst 档叙事：放弃 diagnostic 作为 ''decision tool''，重构为 ''sufficient condition\n    for concern''——当 Δπ×Δτ 非常大时，global correction 肯定有风险 （这是 identity 的直接推论），但 intermediate\n    values 无法可靠区分。这实际上是从 Claim 3 退回到 Claim 1 的推论。\n\n    '\n- name: Expert label budget sensitivity\n  plan_id: exp-006\n  description: 'n_expert × K × regime 的系统性 sweep，找 EC-HTE > Global 的 crossover point。\n    Worst 档下 crossover 要求大量 expert labels，moderate regime 永远不 cross。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    n_mc: 100\n    grid: n_expert=[50,100,250,500,1000,2000] × K=[2,4,8] × regime=[extreme,moderate]\n    crossover_hb_beats_global:\n      K2_extreme: 500\n      K2_moderate: never\n      K4_extreme: 2000\n      K4_moderate: never\n      K8_extreme: never\n      K8_moderate: never\n    hb_vs_mle_pct_configs_hb_wins: 60%\n    hb_vs_mle_max_improvement: +15% RMSE (K4/moderate/n50)\n    ec_hte_rmse_penalty_median: 1.6\n    ec_hte_rmse_penalty_k4_n100: 2.3\n    ec_hte_rmse_penalty_k8_n100: 3.5\n  result_rationale: 'Worst 档假设 ec_hte_rmse_penalty_median 在 [1.3, 2.5]，hb_crossover_k4_moderate\n    = [2000, never]。Crossover points 全面上移：K=2/extreme 从 250 升到 500（需要 双倍 expert labels），K=4/extreme\n    从 1000 升到 2000（接近 impractical），K=4/moderate 和所有 K=8 配置永远不 cross。原因：worst 档下 EC-HTE\n    的 bias 优势本身较弱 （reduction factor 仅 0.8-1.5×），RMSE penalty 更重（per-subgroup CM estimation\n    noise 高），两者叠加导致 crossover 需要更多 data 来 amortize variance cost。 K=8 是 worst 档新增的\n    stress test——8 subgroups 意味着 n_expert/8 极少，CM 估计 完全不可靠。审稿人会指出 ''crossover requires\n    2000 expert labels for K=4 — at that point, why not just use expert labels directly\n    for CATE?''\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Table 8: RMSE crossover n_expert by K × regime'\n    columns:\n    - K\n    - regime\n    - crossover_n\n    - ec_hte_rmse_at_crossover\n    - global_rmse_at_crossover\n    representative_rows:\n    - - 2\n      - extreme\n      - 500\n      - 0.13\n      - 0.132\n    - - 2\n      - moderate\n      - never\n      - —\n      - —\n    - - 4\n      - extreme\n      - 2000\n      - 0.088\n      - 0.09\n    - - 4\n      - moderate\n      - never\n      - —\n      - —\n    - - 8\n      - extreme\n      - never\n      - —\n      - —\n    - - 8\n      - moderate\n      - never\n      - —\n      - —\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Line plot: RMSE vs n_expert for each K, with global as horizontal reference line.\n    EC-HTE curves slowly approach global from above; only K=2/extreme and K=4/extreme\n    eventually cross.'\n  analysis: 'Budget analysis 彻底暴露 EC-HTE 的 practical limitation：在多数现实场景（moderate heterogeneity\n    或 K>4），global correction 始终是更好的选择。EC-HTE 唯一有价值的 scenario 是 extreme heterogeneity\n    + small K + large expert budget——这是一个非常 narrow niche。论文必须 honestly present 这些\n    crossover，强化 ''conditional advantage'' framing。审稿人会用 K=8/never 结果论证 EC-HTE 缺乏\n    scalability。\n\n    '\n- name: PPCI + DSL baseline comparison\n  plan_id: exp-007\n  description: 'PPCI vs EC-HTE vs DSL 在四种 DGP 下的比较。Worst 档下 PPCI 在 DGP A (covariate-only\n    error) 也有 partial correction 能力，削弱 EC-HTE 独特性。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    total_configs: 48\n    mc_runs: 100\n    dgp_a_covariate_only:\n      ec_hte_avg_bias: 0.03\n      ec_hte_avg_rmse: 0.18\n      global_avg_bias: 0.08\n      global_avg_rmse: 0.12\n      ppci_avg_bias: 0.05\n      ppci_avg_rmse: 0.14\n      dsl_per_subgroup_avg_bias: 0.04\n      dsl_per_subgroup_avg_rmse: 0.2\n    dgp_b_outcome_only:\n      ec_hte_avg_bias: 0.08\n      ppci_avg_bias: 0.02\n      global_avg_bias: 0.07\n    dgp_c_both_errors:\n      ec_hte_ppci_avg_bias: 0.008\n      ec_hte_avg_bias: 0.15\n      ppci_avg_bias: 0.06\n      global_avg_bias: 0.12\n    dgp_d_no_error:\n      all_methods_bias: <0.01\n    ec_hte_unique_advantage_over_ppci_dgp_a: bias 0.03 vs 0.05 (40% better, but RMSE\n      29% worse)\n    ppci_partial_covariate_correction: true\n  result_rationale: 'Worst 档下 PPCI 在 DGP A（纯 covariate error）也能 partially correct（bias\n    0.05 vs EC-HTE 0.03）——因为 PPCI rectifier 是 model-free，可以捕获任何 systematic error 包括\n    covariate-side。这削弱了 ''EC-HTE is uniquely needed for covariate error'' 的 论点。EC-HTE\n    仍然 slightly better on bias（0.03 vs 0.05），但 RMSE penalty 使得 net advantage ambiguous。DSL\n    per-subgroup 的 bias 与 EC-HTE comparable（0.04 vs 0.03），验证了审稿人的担忧：''just apply DSL\n    per subgroup, no need for HB''。DGP C 的 composition 仍然有效（ec_hte_ppci bias 0.008），但审稿人会指出\n    PPCI alone 已经 做到 0.06——composition 的 marginal gain 可能不值得复杂度。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Table 9: Method comparison across DGP types (n_expert=250, K=2, extreme)'\n    columns:\n    - dgp\n    - method\n    - avg_abs_bias\n    - avg_rmse\n    - coverage\n    representative_rows:\n    - - A\n      - ec_hte\n      - 0.03\n      - 0.18\n      - 0.93\n    - - A\n      - ppci\n      - 0.05\n      - 0.14\n      - 0.9\n    - - A\n      - dsl_subgroup\n      - 0.04\n      - 0.2\n      - 0.88\n    - - A\n      - global\n      - 0.08\n      - 0.12\n      - 0.82\n    - - B\n      - ec_hte\n      - 0.08\n      - 0.16\n      - 0.9\n    - - B\n      - ppci\n      - 0.02\n      - 0.13\n      - 0.94\n    - - C\n      - ec_hte_ppci\n      - 0.008\n      - 0.2\n      - 0.95\n    - - C\n      - ppci\n      - 0.06\n      - 0.14\n      - 0.91\n    - - C\n      - ec_hte\n      - 0.15\n      - 0.19\n      - 0.88\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Grouped bar chart: |bias| by DGP × method. EC-HTE 优势仅在 DGP A 可见且 modest；PPCI\n    在所有 DGP 都 reasonable。'\n  analysis: 'PPCI 的 partial covariate correction 是 worst 档的关键 negative signal——如果一个\n    通用方法已经能 partially correct covariate error，EC-HTE 的 ''structured correction for\n    covariate error'' 卖点被显著削弱。DSL per-subgroup 作为 simple baseline 表现 surprisingly\n    close to EC-HTE，进一步降低 novelty argument。Composition 仍然 works but marginal gain\n    over PPCI alone 有限。论文需要诚实承认 PPCI 的 partial coverage 并 reframe EC-HTE 的价值为 ''structured\n    + interpretable'' 而非 ''strictly necessary''。\n\n    '\n- name: Multiple LLM annotator comparison\n  plan_id: exp-008\n  description: '多 LLM 比较 misclassification heterogeneity patterns。Worst 档下 heterogeneity\n    存在但 Δπ 较小，EC-HTE benefit 因此更弱。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    models_completed:\n    - gpt-3.5-turbo\n    - gpt-4.1\n    - gpt-4o\n    - gpt-4o-mini\n    - gpt-4-turbo\n    - gpt-5.4\n    effective_delta_pi:\n      gpt-3.5-turbo: 0.15\n      gpt-4-turbo: 0.1\n      gpt-4.1: 0.06\n      gpt-4o: 0.05\n      gpt-4o-mini: 0.09\n      gpt-5.4: 0.05\n    all_delta_pi_above_005: true\n    median_delta_pi: 0.075\n    ec_hte_benefit_prediction: At median Δπ=0.075, expected bias amplification ~1.15×\n      — minimal practical impact\n    worst_subgroup_consensus: True_medium (4/6 models)\n    newer_models_lower_delta_pi: true\n  result_rationale: '所有 LLM 都展示 Δπ > 0.05（heterogeneity 是 structural），但 newer/better\n    models （GPT-4o, GPT-5.4）的 Δπ 更低（~0.05）。这意味着随着 LLM 进步，misclassification heterogeneity\n    自然减小，EC-HTE 的 relevance 随之递减。Worst 档叙事：''EC-HTE solves a problem that is diminishing\n    as LLMs improve''。Median Δπ=0.075 对应的 bias amplification 仅 ~1.15×——审稿人会问 ''is\n    15% amplification worth the complexity of HB correction?''。论文可以 salvage by arguing\n    that even 5% heterogeneity exists and Claim 1 formal characterization remains\n    relevant——但 EC-HTE 的实际价值主张被 削弱。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Table 10: Δπ by LLM model generation'\n    columns:\n    - model\n    - generation\n    - accuracy\n    - delta_pi\n    - predicted_max_amplification\n    representative_rows:\n    - - gpt-3.5-turbo\n      - '3.5'\n      - 0.72\n      - 0.15\n      - 1.8×\n    - - gpt-4-turbo\n      - '4'\n      - 0.81\n      - 0.1\n      - 1.4×\n    - - gpt-4.1\n      - '4.1'\n      - 0.86\n      - 0.06\n      - 1.15×\n    - - gpt-5.4\n      - '5'\n      - 0.9\n      - 0.05\n      - 1.10×\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Line plot: Δπ vs model generation/accuracy. 下降趋势明显——better models → less heterogeneity。'\n  analysis: 'Multi-LLM 结果是 double-edged：确认 heterogeneity 是 universal（所有 LLM 都有）， 但也确认它在\n    diminishing。审稿人可能用 GPT-5.4 的 Δπ=0.05 论证 ''the problem is already mostly solved\n    by better models''。论文可以 counter：(1) 即使 Δπ=0.05， 在 high-stakes CSS 中 any bias matters；(2)\n    less-capable models 仍广泛使用 （cost reasons）；(3) Claim 1 的 formal characterization\n    不取决于 Δπ 大小。\n\n    '\n- name: Adaptive expert annotation allocation\n  plan_id: exp-009\n  description: 'CATE-weighted allocation vs uniform vs uncertainty-only。Worst 档下 adaptive\n    allocation 的改进 negligible。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    allocation_strategies:\n    - uniform\n    - uncertainty_only\n    - cate_weighted\n    - oracle_allocation\n    n_expert: 250\n    K: 4\n    regime: extreme\n    avg_rmse:\n      uniform: 0.175\n      uncertainty_only: 0.17\n      cate_weighted: 0.168\n      oracle_allocation: 0.155\n    avg_bias:\n      uniform: 0.065\n      uncertainty_only: 0.06\n      cate_weighted: 0.058\n      oracle_allocation: 0.045\n    cate_weighted_vs_uniform_rmse_improvement: 4%\n    cate_weighted_vs_uniform_bias_improvement: 11%\n  result_rationale: 'Worst 档下 EC-HTE 本身优势微弱，adaptive allocation 在此基础上进一步优化的空间 很小。CATE-weighted\n    vs uniform 仅 4% RMSE 改进和 11% bias 改进——统计上可能不 significant。原因：(1) 当 EC-HTE 的 bias\n    reduction 本身就 modest 时，optimally allocating labels 的 marginal return 也 modest；(2)\n    CATE heterogeneity 未知（需要 initial estimate），estimation error 吃掉了 allocation gain；(3)\n    K=4 时 subgroup sizes unbalanced，minority subgroups 已经需要所有能得到的 labels，allocation\n    灵活性 有限。P2 priority 合理——这个实验在 worst 档下几乎无论文价值。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Table 11: Allocation strategy comparison (K=4, extreme, n=250)'\n    columns:\n    - strategy\n    - avg_bias\n    - avg_rmse\n    - worst_subgroup_rmse\n    representative_rows:\n    - - uniform\n      - 0.065\n      - 0.175\n      - 0.28\n    - - uncertainty_only\n      - 0.06\n      - 0.17\n      - 0.26\n    - - cate_weighted\n      - 0.058\n      - 0.168\n      - 0.25\n    - - oracle\n      - 0.045\n      - 0.155\n      - 0.2\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Bar chart: RMSE by allocation strategy. 差异非常小，error bars 重叠。'\n  analysis: 'Adaptive allocation 在 worst 档下是 noise。Improvement 太小，不值得 paper space。\n    在 reframed 单 claim 论文中完全删除。\n\n    '\n- name: Robustness to misspecified subgroup structure\n  plan_id: exp-010\n  description: 'EC-HTE 在 subgroup 定义 noisy/misspecified 时的表现。Worst 档下 EC-HTE 对 misspecification\n    敏感。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    noise_levels:\n    - 0\n    - 0.1\n    - 0.25\n    - 0.5\n    K2_ec_hte_rmse:\n    - 0.16\n    - 0.17\n    - 0.19\n    - 0.22\n    K2_global_rmse:\n    - 0.12\n    - 0.12\n    - 0.12\n    - 0.12\n    K4_ec_hte_rmse:\n    - 0.2\n    - 0.22\n    - 0.26\n    - 0.3\n    K4_global_rmse:\n    - 0.14\n    - 0.14\n    - 0.14\n    - 0.14\n    K2_ec_hte_coverage:\n    - 0.93\n    - 0.91\n    - 0.88\n    - 0.86\n    K4_ec_hte_coverage:\n    - 0.92\n    - 0.89\n    - 0.85\n    - 0.82\n    graceful_convergence_at_50pct: false\n    ec_hte_worse_than_global_at_noise_25pct: true\n  result_rationale: 'Worst 档假设 coverage_ec_hte_small_n 在 [0.85, 0.92]。当 subgroup assignment\n    有 noise 时，per-subgroup CM 估计受污染，EC-HTE 的 stratification 变成 liability。 Global correction\n    对 subgroup noise immune（它本来就不 condition on subgroups）。 在 25% noise level，EC-HTE\n    的 RMSE 已经显著劣于 global（K=4: 0.26 vs 0.14）， coverage 跌到 0.85。HB shrinkage 理论上应该 gracefully\n    degrade 但在 worst 档下 concentration prior 不够 strong 来 pull noisy subgroups back\n    to global。这比 actual exp-010 结果（coverage 0.946 at 50% noise）显著差——worst 档假设 HB 实现或\n    prior calibration 有问题。审稿人会用这个结果论证 EC-HTE 在 real settings（subgroups never perfectly\n    known）不可靠。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Table 12: Robustness to subgroup misspecification (K=4, n_expert=250)'\n    columns:\n    - noise_level\n    - ec_hte_rmse\n    - global_rmse\n    - ec_hte_coverage\n    - penalty_ratio\n    representative_rows:\n    - - 0.0\n      - 0.2\n      - 0.14\n      - 0.92\n      - 1.43\n    - - 0.1\n      - 0.22\n      - 0.14\n      - 0.89\n      - 1.57\n    - - 0.25\n      - 0.26\n      - 0.14\n      - 0.85\n      - 1.86\n    - - 0.5\n      - 0.3\n      - 0.14\n      - 0.82\n      - 2.14\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Line plot: RMSE vs noise level for EC-HTE vs global. EC-HTE 斜率陡峭上升，global 平坦。'\n  analysis: 'Robustness results 在 worst 档下是 EC-HTE 的又一 liability。Real-world subgroup\n    definitions 不会是 noise-free，25% misspecification 是 conservative estimate。 EC-HTE\n    的 penalty ratio 从 1.43 增加到 2.14——比 clean 条件下更差。这进一步 限制了 EC-HTE 的 practical applicability。论文需要非常\n    honest 地报告这些结果 并明确 ''EC-HTE requires well-defined subgroups'' 作为 limitation。\n\n    '\n- name: Causal forest integration\n  plan_id: exp-011\n  description: 'CausalForestDML + EC-HTE post-hoc correction。Worst 档下 causal forest\n    放大了 debiasing-hurts effect（支持 Claim 1），但 EC-HTE correction 的 RMSE penalty 更严重。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    n_mc: 100\n    n_configs: 8\n    mean_abs_bias:\n      naive_forest: 0.16\n      global_forest: 0.12\n      ec_hte_forest: 0.08\n    mean_rmse:\n      naive_forest: 0.18\n      global_forest: 0.17\n      ec_hte_forest: 0.28\n    debiasing_hurts_cases: 10\n    debiasing_hurts_max_ratio: 5.2\n    ec_hte_rmse_penalty_vs_global: 1.65\n    ec_hte_forest_coverage: 0.88\n    bias_reduction_factor: 1.5\n  result_rationale: 'Causal forest 放大了 bias mechanism（max ratio 5.2×，因为 tree-based\n    CATE 的 nonlinear estimation 在 subgroup boundaries 处 compounds error），强力支持 Claim\n    1。 但同时 EC-HTE correction 的 RMSE penalty 更重（1.65× vs global），因为 forest pseudo-outcomes\n    已经 noisy，再加上 per-subgroup CM correction noise 叠加。 Coverage 0.88 低于 nominal 95%——forest\n    variance estimation 加 CM uncertainty 的 joint calibration 有问题。Bias reduction factor\n    1.5× 处于 worst 档上限—— EC-HTE 确实 helps on bias 但代价高。这进一步支持 ''reframe around Claim\n    1'' 叙事： CausalForest 使得 debiasing-hurts 更 dramatic（5.2× amplification），但 EC-HTE\n    fix 的 cost 也更高。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Table 13: CausalForest results by K × regime'\n    columns:\n    - K\n    - regime\n    - method\n    - avg_abs_bias\n    - avg_rmse\n    - debiasing_hurts_max_ratio\n    representative_rows:\n    - - 2\n      - extreme\n      - naive_forest\n      - 0.14\n      - 0.17\n      - —\n    - - 2\n      - extreme\n      - global_forest\n      - 0.1\n      - 0.16\n      - 2.8\n    - - 2\n      - extreme\n      - ec_hte_forest\n      - 0.05\n      - 0.24\n      - —\n    - - 4\n      - extreme\n      - naive_forest\n      - 0.18\n      - 0.2\n      - —\n    - - 4\n      - extreme\n      - global_forest\n      - 0.15\n      - 0.18\n      - 5.2\n    - - 4\n      - extreme\n      - ec_hte_forest\n      - 0.09\n      - 0.32\n      - —\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Heatmap: debiasing-hurts ratio by K × subgroup for CausalForest. K=4/extreme/sg0\n    达到 5.2×。'\n  - 'Bias-RMSE scatter: CausalForest methods. EC-HTE 在 bias 轴更好但 RMSE 轴显著更差。'\n  analysis: CausalForest 结果为 Claim 1 提供最强支持——5.2× amplification 是 dramatic 且 practically\n    concerning。但 EC-HTE 的 RMSE penalty (1.65×) 和 undercoverage (0.88) 使得 'the fix\n    is worse than the disease' argument 更 plausible。Worst 档叙事： 'We identify a severe\n    bias mechanism (up to 5.2× with causal forests), but acknowledge that current\n    correction methods trade bias for variance in ways that may not be practically\n    acceptable.' 这支持 reframe 为 negative result paper。\n","numLines":973,"startLine":1,"totalLines":973}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01HxERPtodHAFMvUmoEtNAzq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me carefully review this paper and then prepare a comprehensive review report. Let me first load the required tool schema for submitting the review.\n\nThe paper is: \"Debiasing Can Hurt: When Global Misclassification Correction Amplifies Subgroup CATE Bias\"\n\nLet me analyze the paper against the experiment context (which describes a \"worst\" tier scenario), and then write a thorough review.\n\nKey observations from reading the paper:\n\n**Core claim**: When LLM misclassification rates vary across subgroups, applying a pooled (global) confusion matrix correction to subgroup-level CATE estimates introduces systematic bias proportional to Δπ × Δτ.\n \nThe paper makes several strong contributions: it tackles an underexplored problem in effect-modifier misclassification within heterogeneous treatment effect analysis, derives a clean mathematical characterization of the bias mechanism through the Δπ × Δτ product form, and presents the work with refreshing candor about EC-HTE's limitations and real-world performance. The experimental validation is thorough, spanning synthetic, semi-synthetic, and real datasets across multiple methods and LLM variants. However, the theoretical contribution feels somewhat narrow—the bias identity, while intuitive, is fundamentally a straightforward matrix algebra result—and the practical guidance on when to apply or avoid global correction remains limited.\n\nThe core methodological weakness is that EC-HTE itself doesn't deliver: the paper honestly shows it underperforms on RMSE in most scenarios, demands substantial expert annotation budgets, fails on real data, and gets partially superseded by PPCI anyway. This leaves the paper in an awkward position of proposing a method primarily to demonstrate its shortcomings. Even more problematic is that the diagnostic criterion—the natural practical tool that should follow from the theory—performs at chance level with CV AUC around 0.50, which severely undermines the paper's ability to offer actionable guidance for practitioners.\n\nThe real-world results further complicate the narrative: EC-HTE actually underperforms the global baseline on the UC Berkeley Hate Speech dataset, which reviewers will see as contradicting the practical value despite the paper's attempt to frame it as theoretically consistent. There's also a concerning trend where the magnitude of the problem itself appears to be shrinking—the Δπ effect declines from 0.15 to 0.05 as language models improve across the multi-LLM analysis—raising questions about whether this addresses a transient issue. Finally, the emergence of competing approaches like PPCI and DSL-based per-subgroup methods narrows EC-HTE's unique contribution, since PPCI achieves comparable bias reduction with superior RMSE performance.\n\nBeyond these empirical concerns, the core assumption of non-differential misclassification may be unrealistic for LLMs where errors systematically correlate with outcome-relevant features. The validation is thin—only one real dataset with results that contradict the method—and the headline finding that debiasing helps in roughly 48% of cases reads more like \"sometimes it works, sometimes it doesn't\" than a compelling methodological advance. The paper also tries to pack ten experiments into eight pages, with some (allocation strategies, robustness checks) contributing little and potentially better cut to sharpen the core narrative. Now I'm checking the remaining experiments—allocation and robustness are accounted for, along with the causal forest analysis. All nine experiments are covered across the paper's sections and tables. Looking at how this would score for EMNLP 2026, the ~21% acceptance rate is competitive, but this paper presents honest negative results with only incremental theoretical contributions and weak methodological novelty, which likely puts it in borderline Findings territory rather than Main conference material.\n\nAssessing the soundness, excitement, and reproducibility: the theory checks out and experiments are thorough, though the assumptions are restrictive and real-world evidence undermines the method. The problem itself feels less urgent as language models improve. The EC-HTE approach simply doesn't perform well empirically, which shows integrity but leaves the paper without a compelling contribution. Reproducibility is solid with clear experimental details, though code availability isn't mentioned. Overall this lands around 2.5—the theoretical identity is correct but incremental compared to prior work, and the proposed method's failure, while honestly reported, doesn't provide enough value to overcome the limitations. Though reconsidering, there are genuine strengths here worth acknowledging.\n\nThe paper does address a real gap that nobody's tackled before—effect-modifier misclassification in CATE estimation. The formal framework is clean, the transparency about negative results is refreshing, and the causal forest amplification effect of 5.2× is genuinely alarming. The experimental scope is comprehensive. For a venue like EMNLP, negative results that protect practitioners from mistakes have real value, and the formal characterization gives researchers a concrete way to reason about when this problem matters. Even if EC-HTE itself is weak, the diagnostic contribution stands on its own. Still, the amplification in the moderate regime only reaches 1.1-1.5×, which many would dismiss as negligible.\n\nThe extreme cases showing 2.5× and 5.2× amplification are concerning but narrow in scope, the diagnostic doesn't generalize well, and Carroll et al. already established the underlying principle. I'm settling on 2.5 for overall quality, with soundness at 3.5, excitement at 2.0, and reproducibility at 3.5. Now I'll draft and submit the review.","signature":""}]